Now, the problem says that Mike can fit 9 books on a shelf. The question is asking how many shelves he will need. Hmm, so if each shelf holds 9 books, I need to divide the number of books he has by the number of books per shelf. That would be 72 divided by 9. Let me do that division. 72 divided by 9... Well, 9 times 8 is 72, right? So 72 divided by 9 is exactly 8. 

