To figure this out, let's start with the total candy she had at first, which is 47 pieces. Then, we subtract the 25 pieces she ate the first night. That would be 47 minus 25. Let's do the subtraction. 47 minus 25 is 22. So, after eating the first night, she had 22 pieces of candy left.

Next, her sister gave her 40 more pieces of candy. So, we need to add those 40 pieces to the 22 pieces she had left. That would be 22 plus 40. Let's do the addition. 22 plus 40 is 62. So, after her sister gave her more candy, Faye has 62 pieces of candy now.

Therefore, Faye now has 62 pieces of candy.
