Now, she wants to divide these 48 pieces into piles with 8 in each pile. So the question is, how many piles of 8 can she make from 48? That seems like a division problem. So I need to divide 48 by 8. Let me do that. 48 divided by 8... Well, 8 times 6 is 48, right? 8 times 5 is 40, plus 8 is 48. So that's 6. Therefore, she can make 6 piles.

