But wait, the problem says he used the money he earned from selling the books to buy 30 new books. So, the money from selling the 21 books allows him to buy 30 new ones. So, does that mean he adds 30 books to his remaining 4? 

So, after selling, he has 4 books, and then he buys 30 new ones. So, 4 plus 30 would be... 34. Therefore, Roger would have 34 books in total. 

Let me just check again. He starts with 25, sells 21, so 25 -21=4 left. Then he uses the money to buy 30 new books. So adding those to his remaining 4. 4+30=34. Yeah, that seems right. 

