Now, she's putting these 45 files into folders, each folder holding 5 files. So, to find out how many folders she needs, I need to divide the total number of remaining files by the number of files per folder. That would be 45 divided by 5. Let me do that division. 45 divided by 5 is 9. So, that suggests she ends up with 9 folders.

Wait, let me check again. If each folder has 5 files, then 5 files per folder times 9 folders would be 45 files total. And 85 minus 40 is indeed 45. So that seems to add up. 

